-- title:
--   Ends off N are the affine places, moved by the level
-- statement:
--   Let $q\ge 5$ be a prime and $M'\ge 1$ with $q\nmid M'$, let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with residue field $\kappa$, and let $F_{ss}$ be a field with a $\kappa$-algebra structure. Let $R$ be a regular prolongation of $A$ to `fieldBar q M'`, the function field over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the modular curve $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$ for $H$ the kernel of $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, with residue field $F_{ss}$: thus a valuation subring `R.integers` of that field, a surjective ring map onto $F_{ss}$ with kernel its maximal ideal, lying over $A$ and compatible with $\kappa$, together with the scaling property that every nonzero $f$ has a multiple $c\cdot f$ integral with nonzero residue. Let $N$ be a finite set of places of $F_{ss}$ over $\kappa$ (valuation subrings $\ne\top$ containing $\kappa$ and principal), subject to: `R.integers` is preserved by pullback along every level automorphism `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and $\zeta$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity; $\#N=q+1$; and each $\tau$ in the group generated by those level automorphisms, when it preserves `R.integers`, induces a residue automorphism `R.resAut` whose action on places preserves $N$. Assume further a $\mathbb F_{q^2}$-algebra structure on $\kappa$, that the Drinfeld coordinate ring [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) (the quotient of $\kappa[X_0,X_1]$ by `drinfeldPoly q κ - 1`) is a domain, and fix $\zeta$, a subgroup $C_s\le\mu_{q+1}(\mathbb F_{q^2})$ and a $\kappa$-algebra isomorphism $e$ from $F_{ss}$ onto the fixed field [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q κ Cs`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32) of $C_s$ acting on the Drinfeld function field $\operatorname{Frac}(\mathrm{CoordRing})$; assume $e$ intertwines the residue automorphism of `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹` with `hFunctionFieldAction` at $(\gamma \bmod q,1)$, for every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ for which that pair lies in `hSubgroup q`, the kernel of $(g,u)\mapsto \det(g)\,u^{q+1}$. The conclusion is twofold: first, a place $Q$ of $F_{ss}$ over $\kappa$ lies outside $N$ if and only if $e^{-1}(z)$ lies in the valuation subring of $Q$ for every $z$ in the fixed field whose image in the Drinfeld function field comes from the coordinate ring; second, every $Q\notin N$ satisfies `R.resAut (levelAutBar q M' ζ γ) • Q ≠ Q` for some $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ whose level automorphism preserves `R.integers`.
--
--   Under the identification of the supersingular component of the stable reduction with a quotient of the Drinfeld curve $xy^q-x^qy=1$, this identifies the distinguished set $N$ of $q+1$ places with the places at infinity (the ends of the component), the complement being the affine places, and records that no affine place is fixed by the whole level group. It feeds the transitivity statement [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.supersingularProlongation_levelAut_transitive_ends_moves_smoothPlaces`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.supersingularProlongation_levelAut_transitive_ends_moves_smoothPlaces), which uses the census of places at infinity of the Drinfeld quotient, the surjectivity of $\Gamma_0(M')\to SL_2(\mathbb F_q)$, and the freeness of the action on affine places.
